    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44750" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŏphos</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŏphus</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a wise man</i>, <i>sage</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">te sophos omnis amat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 32, 4</span></i>
			.—Adjectively, <i>wise</i>, <i>shrewd</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">victor sophus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 3, 14, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">factus periclo tum gubernator sophus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					4, 15, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
